  "summary": "A state-sponsored public art movement using monumental walls to narrate history, labor and indigenous identity.",
  "description": "After the Mexican Revolution, José Vasconcelos's ministry commissioned Rivera, Orozco and Siqueiros to paint civic murals for public buildings. The movement fused European modernism with pre-Hispanic visual traditions, favoring dynamic compositions, monumental figures, earthy palettes and political narrative. It influenced public art programs across the Americas and the WPA. Its didactic monumentalism remains a reference for socially engaged visual culture.",
